# Rust build output
target/
**/target/

# Tauri
/src-tauri/target/

# Node
node_modules/
dist/

# Python (tools/ scripts import each other)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local data
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Reference material, not managed by git: the UCS release folder is downloaded
# by hand and read by `tools/import-ucs.py`, which writes the committed
# `tools/ucs_keywords.py`. The release itself is never redistributed.
/docs/UCS Release/

# Tauri generated ACL schemas. Regenerated by `tauri-build` on every compile, so
/src-tauri/gen/
# they are build output, not source. Both the probe window and the product shell
# put them in `crates/*/gen/` or `probes/*/src-tauri/gen/`.
gen/schemas/
**/gen/schemas/
probes/**/src-tauri/gen/

# Testlist
/docs/test-list.md

# Logo files. The design source and its exports stay on this machine: the icon
# set they produced is committed in `crates/mio-app/icons/` and the top-bar mark
# in `ui/src/assets/brand.svg`, and neither build step reads this directory. A
# fresh clone therefore cannot re-run `tools/make-app-icon.py` — that is the
# intended trade, not an oversight.
logo/
